1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The Advanced Test Reactor.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Predictions of the lifetime characteristics of materials operating in a reactor environment

3
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:50,000
is made possible by accelerated irradiation in test reactors.

4
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:59,000
One of the first test reactors is the 40 megawatt materials testing reactor.

5
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,000
This design achieves neutron fluxes of 3 times 10 to the 14th fast neutrons per square centimeter

6
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:14,000
per second.

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,000
The 175 megawatt engineering test reactor attains fluxes of 9 times 10 to the 14th fast

8
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:30,000
neutrons per square centimeter per second.

9
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
The ATR will provide even more severe test environments.

10
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The ATR uses the flux trap concept, which produces high flux in an experimental region

11
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
surrounded by fuel.

12
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Placing several of these flux traps in a single pressure vessel is a logical extension of

13
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
this concept.

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Economies are possible by combining five flux traps in a single core with one control system

15
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
and one set of auxiliary hardware.

16
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Finally, a serpentine fuel configuration evolves, providing multiple flux traps in an efficient

17
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
circular geometry.

18
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:28,000
The ATR will operate at 250 thermal megawatts, achieving experimental peak fast fluxes of

19
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:35,000
1.5 times 10 to the 15th fast neutrons per square centimeter per second.

20
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:44,000
There are five 50 megawatt fuel regions, the four lobes, and the center region.

21
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The core configuration provides nine six-inch flux traps.

22
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Each trap surrounds an experiment pressure tube.

23
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,000
The flux spectrum in any trap can be modified by changing the composition of the moderating

24
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:14,000
material. Lobe power can be varied from 40 to 60 megawatts. This power tilt is

25
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:18,000
achieved principally by rotating beryllium shim cylinders which have a

26
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:25,000
hafnium plate covering one-third of their surfaces. As the cylinders are

27
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:31,000
rotated, the desirable constant vertical cosine flux distribution is maintained.

28
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:38,000
As fuel is consumed, power distribution is maintained by further movement of the cylinders

29
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:42,000
and of hapnium-necked shim rods.

30
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Individual rods are either fully in or out, and do not alter vertical flux distribution.

31
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:59,000
To achieve its advanced performance, the ATR uses special fuel, control components and

32
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:04,000
support structures.

33
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:09,000
A major vertical support and alignment structure is the aluminum neck shim housing, which is

34
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:15,000
drilled to receive haptium shim rods.

35
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:19,000
It supports the flux trap baffle tubes.

36
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:26,000
The baffle tubes surround each of the nine experiment pressure tubes.

37
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Cylindrical safety rods surround the pressure tubes.

38
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:34,000
The rods have an upper hafnium poison section.

39
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Removable inserts in the follower are used to vary the neutron moderation.

40
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:47,000
The rods are driven from below the core by a rack and pinion.

41
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
operation the poison section is above the core, the aluminum follower is in the

42
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:58,000
flux trap region. When the reactor is scrammed, the rods drop under the

43
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:05,000
combined action of gravity, spring, and hydraulic forces. Safety rods can be

44
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:10,000
placed in any one of eight positions. On the basis of critical tests, only five

45
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
safety rods are installed.

46
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
The 24 hafnium neck shim rods are driven from below.

47
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Two rods are used to provide fine regulating control.

48
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
The other neck rods are used as full-in or full-out shim rods.

49
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
The 16 outer shim cylinders operate in pairs.

50
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:57,000
They are driven from above the core.

51
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:05,000
The fuel annulus is made up of 40 elements, each 48 inches long.

52
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Each 45 degree fuel element sector contains 19 equally spaced curved plates.

53
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:18,000
The aluminum clad fuel is uranium oxide dispersed in an aluminum matrix and contains boron carbide

54
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:28,000
as burnable poison.

55
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:32,000
The complete core is surrounded by a beryllium reflector.

56
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:38,000
The holes in the reflector are used for static irradiation experiments.

57
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:42,000
The core assembly is contained within a cylindrical aluminum tank,

58
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:51,000
supported through a series of tanks from the reactor pressure vessel bottom head.

59
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Water coolant enters the lower part of the reactor vessel,

60
00:06:55,000 --> 00:07:01,000
upward through the thermal shields and then flows downward through the core and

61
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:10,000
reflector. The coolant is then diverted to four 16-inch outlet pipes. Test

62
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:16,000
specimens may be irradiated in loops using water, gases, or liquid metal

63
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:21,000
coolants at temperatures and pressures expected in the most advanced power

64
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
reactors.
